      "post" : {
        "tags" : [ "objects" ],
        "summary" : "Resolve an Incident, Alert or Case",
        "operationId" : "postObjectsByObjectIdResolve",
        "description" : "The fixed `resolve` action (WS-10). An Incident resolves only with a `disposition` from the Disposition ladder — absent or unknown is 422, as is any other gap of the resolution gate (timeline, cause analysis, corrective actions, SLA). A `disposition` on a non-Incident is 422: a Case records its Disposition in its Findings. Reopening an Incident clears the recorded disposition, so the next resolve must decide again.",
